---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Third Room"
  description="What Third Room is: a long-term archive of serious public philosophy."
  current="about"
>
  <article class="container narrow">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">A place for serious public philosophy.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-block prose">
      <p>
        Third Room is a long-term archive—not a social product. The aim is a
        permanent, well-organized collection of live discussions, written
        summaries, podcast episodes, and essays that stay useful years after
        they appear.
      </p>
      <p>
        Think library or journal energy: clarity over cleverness, ideas over
        personalities, permanence over virality.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-block prose">
      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Events</strong> — live Saturday calls (online)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Discussions</strong> — written summaries after each event
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Podcasts</strong> — audio episodes after each event
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Articles</strong> — standalone essays, added one by one
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Topics</strong> — hubs that group related content by subject
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Nothing important should exist only in a Zoom recording or a chat
        thread. Every discussion should leave an artifact.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-block prose">
      <h2>Cadence</h2>
      <p>
        Discussions run on <strong>Saturdays at 12:00 noon IST</strong>, online.
        About four events per month. Recurring series:
        <a href={`${base}topics/vegan-philosophy/`}>Vegan Philosophy</a>,
        <a href={`${base}topics/atheism-philosophy-of-religion/`}
          >Atheism &amp; Philosophy of Religion</a
        >,
        <a href={`${base}topics/continental-philosophy/`}
          >Continental Philosophy</a
        >, and
        <a href={`${base}topics/indian-philosophy/`}>Indian Philosophy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        See <a href={`${base}events/`}>upcoming events</a> to join the next
        conversation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-block prose">
      <h2>How to participate</h2>
      <p>
        Register via the Google Form on the event page (name and email). Add the
        session to your calendar, and use the Zoom link when it is posted.
        Barrier stays low—no accounts required.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
